cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SemAlign-TS in your research, please cite this software and the accompanying paper."
title: "SemAlign-TS: Observable Semantic Alignment for Controllable Text-to-Time-Series Generation"
version: 1.0.0
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Ji
    given-names: Hongbang
  - family-names: Tao
    given-names: Jiayi
  - family-names: Sun
    given-names: Leilei
  - family-names: Han
    given-names: Liangzhe
  - family-names: Zhu
    given-names: Tongyu

abstract: >-
  SemAlign-TS is a diffusion-based framework for controllable
  text-to-time-series generation. It formulates generation as a
  closed-loop PLAN-GENERATE-VERIFY-ALIGN process and introduces
  Observable Semantic Relative Alignment (OSRA) to align generated
  trajectories with observable temporal semantics including trend,
  volatility, and peak location.

keywords:
  - time series generation
  - text-to-time-series
  - controllable generation
  - diffusion models
  - semantic alignment

repository-code: "https://github.com/SemAlign-TS/SemAlign-TS"
